Master Node-

1) create the worker ec2 instance as Master node
2) install the jenkins on Master node
3) create the public and private key
   ssh-keygen -t rsa
4) cat the id_rsa and id_rsa.pub 

Agent Node- 
1) login to the ec2 instance as agent node/ worker node
2) add the private key of master (id_rsa) in the .ssh/autherized_keys
3) install the same version of java in both worker and master
4) change the permission of authorized_keys and .ssh file itself.

Master Node - 

1) ssh -i private_key ubuntu@ip of worker
2) open jenkins-
   1) setup the node name
   2) setup remote directory where workspace and all needed file save in worker node
   3) label the node
   4) use the launch method as SSH 
   5) choose host as public ip of agent
   6) in Credentials paste the private key
   7) check worker node is loged in via SSH in log of node
   8) run the pipeline script with just agent {label 'worker-node-1"}

